{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791790011,"nonce":"lSu1dmAFwPgRFnsGYFsjogCnNno=","message":"Decision: no pre-call reservation row for the kill-mid-call case; documented in help costs-and-credits.md and the deep_score docstring instead. Reason: llm_spend is a daily rollup keyed (day, model, tier) with no per-call identity, so a reservation needs a new table plus a reconciler; the real usage of a stream cut off by a kill cannot be fetched afterwards (usage arrives only in the stream, the Messages API has no per-request usage lookup, and the Admin usage API needs an admin key and is aggregated), so reconciliation could only guess; booking the worst case (about 0.83 USD) would overstate a typical 0.05 USD call about 16x and block the rest of a day's deep runs under the default 2 USD cap. The loss is bounded: calls run one at a time and each is admitted only when the cap covers its worst case, so at most one call per kill goes unrecorded. Can be revisited with a deep_request in-flight column if the user wants a conservative booking.","files":null}]}